==English==

===Etymology===
{{prefix|en|di|gloss1=two|cotyledon|gloss2=embryonic leaf}}

===Noun===
{{examples|beans, buttercups, oaks and sunflowers}}
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|botany}} A plant whose [[seedling]] has two [[cotyledon]]s.
#: '''''Dicotyledons''' and monocotyledons together make up the flowering plants, the angiosperms.''
# {{lb|en|botany|historical}} Any plant in what used to be the ''[[Dicotyledones]]''.

